GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets

### Register a user, then copy the returned token into the Authorization headers below
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "7artanis@gmail.com",
  "password": "replace-with-a-12-character-password"
}

### Login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "7artanis@gmail.com",
  "password": "replace-with-a-12-character-password"
}

### Refresh an expired access token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "paste-refresh-token-here"
}

### Create restricted worker tokens using a normal user access token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/worker-token
Authorization: Bearer paste-user-access-token-here

### Save Bitunix credentials for the logged-in user
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/me/exchange-credentials
Authorization: Bearer paste-access-token-here
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "apiKey": "your-bitunix-api-key",
  "apiSecret": "your-bitunix-api-secret"
}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "BTCUSDT"
}
